/** @page ssh2thread_safetyguide Thread Safety

    @tableofcontents

    All classes in this module (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client "SSH2Client", @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient "SFTPClient", and @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel "SSH2Channel") are thread-safe. Internal locking ensures that concurrent access from multiple threads is handled correctly.

    However, note the following considerations:
    - A single connection should not be shared across threads for performance-critical operations, as thread contention may occur
    - @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel "SSH2Channel" objects are tied to their parent @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client "SSH2Client" or @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient "SFTPClient" connection and share the same lock
    - For high-throughput scenarios, consider using separate connection objects per thread
*/
